WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:03.880
A finale that negated 9 seasons of storytelling.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.630
A superhero undone by beer.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.570
The most dramatic haircut ever seen on teen
TV.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:15.799
Even the most celebrated shows can miss the
mark, but these disastrous episodes nearly

00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:18.980
tanked their entire series.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:23.961
After a critically acclaimed debut season,
Friday Night Lights kicked off Season 2 with

00:00:23.961 --> 00:00:25.980
an underwhelming premier.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.220
When Landry whacks Tyra's creepy attacker
with a pipe and dumps his body in a river,

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.910
a respectable show depicting an otherwise
nuanced and realistic depiction of Texas life

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.800
turned into an over-the-top melodrama for
two of its characters.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.480
Actors Jesse Plemons and Adrianne Palicki
do a decent enough job with the material,

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.980
but this bizarre subplot belongs in another
show.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.240
If we wanted to see this kind of death and
a slowly unraveling cover-up, we would have

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.860
tuned in to a soap opera.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.530
The killing of the random stalker guy screamed
network interference and distracted viewers

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.150
from the other parts of the story.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:03.780
Who cares that Coach Taylor has to end his
paternity leave or that Julie feels hemmed

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.100
in by her first serious relationship when
there's a dead body in the river?

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.360
Friday Night Lights would eventually resolve
the subplot with relatively little consequence

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:18.120
and go on to earn its place in our hearts,
but Season 2 opener "Last Days of Summer"

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.490
remains its low point.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.121
In retrospect, Battlestar Galactica would
have been even better if it hadn't been so

00:01:24.121 --> 00:01:28.520
committed to the old model of the 22-episode
season, as it tended to have a couple of random

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.290
filler episodes each year.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:35.130
No episode is more skippable than Season 2's
"Black Market," which seems like a classic

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:38.320
case of writers trying to fit a square peg
into a round hole.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.650
The episode is about an investigation into
an off-book black market that's supposedly

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.310
impossible to corral.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.909
When Commander Fisk is found dead, Captain
Apollo begins digging and discovers that Fisk

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:51.140
was involved in the black market.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.490
After nearly thirty episodes of the show,
we learn that Apollo has a long-lost love

00:01:55.490 --> 00:02:00.180
from back home that he's never once mentioned
and a relationship with a sex worker that

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.180
he regularly sees in the fleet, despite his
tension with Starbuck.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.630
At the end of the episode, after killing a
couple of gangsters, he allows the rest of

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:12.290
the villains to keep doing their black market
thing so long as they stop killing ship commanders

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.329
and trafficking humans.

00:02:14.329 --> 00:02:19.249
"So you're still in business, for now."

00:02:19.249 --> 00:02:24.680
It's a thoroughly nonsensical episode, one
so bad that Battlestar Galactica had to pull

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:29.890
out all the stops with the brilliant, season-ending
time jump on New Caprica to make us forget

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.209
it.

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:34.639
Stranger Things is lucky that it came out
in the era of streaming.

00:02:34.639 --> 00:02:38.719
If fans had been forced to wait an entire
week after the Season 2 episode "The Lost

00:02:38.719 --> 00:02:40.579
Sister," they might have revolted.

00:02:40.579 --> 00:02:45.319
Every season of Stranger Things has replicated
the formula of the first, with varying degrees

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:46.319
of success.

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:51.409
Co-creators Matt and Ross Duffer are pros
at stretching a feature film-worthy adventure

00:02:51.409 --> 00:02:53.760
into eight or nine hours of television.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:59.269
By Episode 7, we're usually hurtling towards
some big confrontation, but "The Lost Sister"

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:04.379
halted that momentum to follow Eleven on a
standalone side quest to Chicago to reconnect

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:08.319
with another experimentee from her past.

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:10.189
"Sister."

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.059
"Sister."

00:03:12.059 --> 00:03:17.020
She ends up with slightly enhanced powers
and a cool new goth vibe, but not much else

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.489
of relevance happens.

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:23.540
It's a complete wrench in what was a well-oiled,
binge-worthy machine of a show.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:28.900
In a world where Stranger Things aired weekly
on cable, fans would have spent seven long

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.120
days seething.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:36.299
Luckily, all they had to do was take a deep
breath and let Netflix play Episode 8 automatically.

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:40.639
NBC's ER was once the epitome of prestige
network drama.

00:03:40.639 --> 00:03:44.879
It was a serious, gripping portrayal of the
passionate people saving lives in a Chicago

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:46.180
emergency room.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:51.120
While it dabbled in the occasional ratings
stunt with plotlines involving escaped convicts,

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.089
serial killers, or George Clooney rescuing
a kid trapped in a storm drain, it generally

00:03:55.089 --> 00:03:59.580
aimed for a realistic, grounded sense of what
life working in a hospital would be like.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.349
As the years went on, the cast changed and
the writers needed to up the ante.

00:04:03.349 --> 00:04:08.810
In the Season 10 episode "Freefall," Dr. Romano
is crushed by a falling helicopter in an impossibly

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.939
slow scene with hilariously bad CGI, even
for 2003.

00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:18.209
This came after Dr. Romano had an arm cut
off by a helicopter rotor in the previous

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:19.209
season.

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:24.450
ER would run for 15 seasons in total, so "Freefall"
didn't outright ruin it.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:28.340
However, the helicopter sequence did make
the show much more difficult to take seriously

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:29.610
from that point on.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:35.159
In truth, any episode from Community Season
4 would be right at home on this list.

00:04:35.159 --> 00:04:39.992
Creator Dan Harmon got forced out by NBC after
Season 3, but the show continued for an entire

00:04:39.992 --> 00:04:42.240
season before he got reinstated.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.690
It retained most of the writing staff, but
they took the show in a lighter, safer direction,

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:47.940
and it was terrible.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:52.900
"Intro to Felt Surrogacy," an episode that
utilized puppets of the main cast, felt like

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:58.099
a pale imitation of the claymation episode
from Season 2, "Abed's Uncontrollable Christmas."

00:04:58.099 --> 00:05:02.460
Another low point was "Heroic Origins," in
which Abed discovers the group had all crossed

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:06.830
paths before meeting at Greendale, essentially
retconning the pilot episode.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.419
"These aren't plot holes, Abed, this is my
life."

00:05:09.419 --> 00:05:11.979
"This kind of connection only makes our origin
story more compelling."

00:05:11.979 --> 00:05:17.450
The lowest low point was "Economics of Marine
Biology," the poorest-rated "Community" episode

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:21.000
on IMDb with a score of just 6.7.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.840
It centers around the college getting ready
to woo a potential new student with lots of

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:25.840
money.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.830
Den of Geek observed that this episode's plotline
was incredibly formulaic, which "makes for

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.590
very bland television."

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:39.590
Even by the standards of Lost's notoriously
convoluted Season 3, "Stranger in a Strange

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:44.189
Land" might be the most inconsequential, pointless
episode of the show.

00:05:44.189 --> 00:05:48.280
Some mildly gripping nonsense with the Others
happens on the island, while the flashbacks

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:54.060
clue viewers in on a mystery nobody was wondering
about: What is the meaning behind Jack's terrible

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.060
tattoos?

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:59.389
In a painfully pointless series of events,
Jack has a brief fling with a mysterious tattoo

00:05:59.389 --> 00:06:01.849
artist in Thailand and then gets beaten up.

00:06:01.849 --> 00:06:04.680
In the present, we learn what his ink translates
to:

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:10.229
"He walks amongst us, but he is not one of
us.

00:06:10.229 --> 00:06:12.740
Your tattoos — that's what they say."

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:17.849
This wording is parallel to how the Bible
describes Jesus as "in the world, but not

00:06:17.849 --> 00:06:18.849
of the world."

00:06:18.849 --> 00:06:23.289
However, the writers leave it unclear as to
whether the tattoo has a similarly spiritual

00:06:23.289 --> 00:06:26.750
meaning, or if the tattoo artist just marked
Jack as a tourist.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:32.219
Either way, "Stranger in a Strange Land" is
an hour that even the biggest Lost fans wanted

00:06:32.219 --> 00:06:33.669
back.

00:06:33.669 --> 00:06:38.199
After nine years, How I Met Your Mother delivered
a polarizing finale.

00:06:38.199 --> 00:06:41.919
While it was clear that future Ted telling
a rambling story to his children was just

00:06:41.919 --> 00:06:45.909
a fun framework for the show, it didn't mean
that fans weren't invested in the resolution

00:06:45.909 --> 00:06:47.669
of Ted and Tracy's relationship.

00:06:47.669 --> 00:06:51.729
The showrunners underestimated how much ire
the finale would generate by killing off the

00:06:51.729 --> 00:06:57.419
mother minutes after she and Ted finally meet,
only to pawn future Ted off on the still magically

00:06:57.419 --> 00:06:58.560
single Robin.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.670
"The point of the story is that—"

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.879
"Is that you totally, totally, totally have
the hots for Aunt Robin."

00:07:03.879 --> 00:07:08.139
Whether or not it was planned all along, it
turned what should have been a perfect landing

00:07:08.139 --> 00:07:12.759
from a beloved show into a bewildering re-framing
of the entire story.

00:07:12.759 --> 00:07:17.199
How I Met Your Mother hasn't enjoyed the resurgence
in popularity that other staples like Friends

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:21.509
and The Office have on streaming services,
but the Hulu spinoff How I Met Your Father

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:25.729
proves that its legacy nonetheless survived
the hit.

00:07:25.729 --> 00:07:30.840
Even the most beloved shows have episodes
that fans always tend to skip, and "The Great

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.590
Divide" is the ultimate proof of that.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:38.910
This much-derided episode of Avatar: The Last
Airbender suffers from being an entirely parenthetical

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:43.810
entry with no relevance to any serial plot,
as two bickering clans argue about how to

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:45.659
cross a vast canyon.

00:07:45.659 --> 00:07:49.979
These tribes were never featured in the main
story before this episode, and they were never

00:07:49.979 --> 00:07:56.120
seen again, making the whole plotline a waste
of time for both the showrunners and viewers.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.629
As if to try and justify the episode's existence,
our heroes get caught up in this petty drama

00:08:00.629 --> 00:08:04.999
and start acting out of character in ways
that shoehorn moral lessons into a show that's

00:08:04.999 --> 00:08:07.529
otherwise known for restraint and subtlety.

00:08:07.529 --> 00:08:12.900
Aang resorts to deception, while Katara and
Sokka each sympathize with a separate tribe.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:16.810
"The Great Divide" seems like it was written
by someone that hadn't seen the rest of the

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:21.499
show, and fans continue to unite in critiquing
it.

00:08:21.499 --> 00:08:27.159
Beloved as it is, Buffy the Vampire Slayer
isn't a show famed for its consistency.

00:08:27.159 --> 00:08:31.570
It often relied on monster-of-the-week style
episodes that were self-contained and not

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:36.890
connected to each season's Big Bad, meaning
it would usually have a few duds per year.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:41.860
Season 4's "Beer Bad" comes across more like
an after school special about the dangers

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:46.240
of alcohol than a fun installment for the
classic urban fantasy series.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:52.460
An enchanted beer causes Buffy to devolve
into a primal, urge-based version of herself.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.810
"Want more singing.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:55.820
Want more beer."

00:08:55.820 --> 00:09:01.400
In her enchantedly drunken state, Buffy starts
to draw cave paintings on her dorm room wall.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:05.500
This is all supposedly meant to illustrate
how upset Buffy is about being dumped by some

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.500
jerk.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.440
The story ends abruptly, without any consequences
for the bartender that drugged a bunch of

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.030
teenagers with magic beer.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:16.540
"Beer Bad" is bad TV, pure and simple.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:20.350
The first season of Parks and Recreation is
nothing like the rest of the show.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:25.120
The main character, Amy Poehler's Leslie Knope,
was essentially an even more boorish and awkward

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:29.160
version of Michael Scott from The Office,
which it was clearly trying to imitate.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:34.451
The show had only a distant echo of the earnestness
it would come to be known for, and if it had

00:09:34.451 --> 00:09:38.290
been canceled before Season 2, nobody would
have batted an eyelid.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:42.900
"Rock Show," the final episode of Season 1,
veered into slapstick territory.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:48.280
Mark gets rejected by a very angry Ann then
makes a drunken attempt to kiss Leslie before

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:49.880
falling into a pit.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:55.750
It's a weird and cringe-worthy end to a season
that hit all the wrong notes, and could easily

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:58.060
have been the last straw for the series.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:02.130
NBC, of course, gave it another shot, and
the subsequent six seasons will live in the

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:04.950
hearts of viewers forever.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:09.120
Most millennials remember Felicity, a show
about the college life of Keri Russell's curly-haired

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.570
eponymous character.

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:14.650
They also likely remember that in the Season
2 episode "The List," Felicity cut her famous

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:18.980
hair on a whim, causing shock and outrage
in equal measure.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:23.730
Felicity's famous locks were part of her character,
and when she said goodbye to them, some fans

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:27.450
said goodbye to the show, seeing it as the
end of a chapter.

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:32.200
What got lost in the reaction to Felicity's
pixie cut is that a sudden, dramatic haircut

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:36.400
is a pretty reasonable reaction to a breakup
like the one she has with Ben in the same

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:37.400
episode.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:41.900
Thankfully, Felicity survived the dramatic
haircut and went on to detail all four years

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:44.150
of our heroine's college experience.

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:49.160
The final season would end with a multi-episode
time travel arc that's far more unique and

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:53.340
memorable than the close-up snipping of some
scissors.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.670
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:58.970
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
shows are coming soon.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.690
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

